#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:69
msgid "The banner works as soon as the plugin is active. These steps take about ten minutes and give you a complete setup."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:71
msgid "Scan your website."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:71
msgid "Cookies → Scan now. Well-known cookies are sorted into the right category automatically."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:72
msgid "Review what was not recognised."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:72
msgid "Cookies → Needs your review: choose a category and click Approve, or Ignore what is not part of your website."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:73
msgid "Create the Cookie Policy page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:73
msgid "Dashboard → Needs your attention → Create the page. It lists your cookies and updates itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:74
msgid "Make the banner yours."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:74
msgid "Banner: position, style, colours, texts and the link to your Privacy Policy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:75
msgid "Check Google."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:75
msgid "If you use Google Analytics or Google Ads, keep Google Consent Mode on (Settings → Blocking and Google)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:76
msgid "Test it like a visitor."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:76
msgid "Open your website in a private window, click a button, then look for the new record in Consent Records."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:84
msgid "A visitor arrives"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:85
msgid "They see your banner. Until they choose, every non-essential script, video, map and font on the page stays switched off. Only the Necessary ones run."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:88
msgid "They make a choice"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:89
msgid "Allow all, Deny, or switch on the categories they want and click Allow selection. What they allowed switches on immediately, without reloading the page. Closing or ignoring the banner never counts as a yes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:92
msgid "The choice is remembered and recorded"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:93
msgid "It is stored in a small cookie called sccm_consent with a unique consent ID, and saved in Consent Records as proof. The visitor can see their consent ID and banner version, and change their choice at any time with the cookie settings button."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:96
msgid "Your cookie list keeps itself current"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:97
msgid "Scans look at your pages; real visitors' browsers can report cookies too. Well-known cookies are sorted automatically, anything else waits for you. Visitors see the list in the Details tab of the banner and on your Cookie Policy page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:100
msgid "It works with page caching"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:101
msgid "Every visitor gets the same page; the banner and the visitor's choice are handled in their browser. When you save settings or the cookie list changes, the plugin clears the page cache of WP Engine, NitroPack, WP Rocket, LiteSpeed, W3 Total Cache, WP Super Cache, WP Fastest Cache, SiteGround, Breeze and Hummingbird. With any other cache or a CDN, clear it once after a change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:114
msgid "A short to-do list, shown only when something is to do. Each line says what is missing and has one button to fix it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:115
msgid "Whether the banner is live, Google Consent Mode, the privacy signal and the current banner version. Preview banner opens your website with the banner showing, even if you already chose yourself. Switch off turns the whole system off: no banner, nothing blocked (the Dashboard then shows a Switch on button first)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:116
msgid "When your website was last scanned, what was found, what waits for your review and when the next automatic scan runs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:117
msgid "Visitor choices"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:117
msgid "How visitors answered in the last 30 days: a chart per day and the share of each answer. \"Allowed all\" is the acceptance rate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:118
msgid "Out of all choices, how many allowed Preferences, Statistics and Marketing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:119
msgid "How many cookies your banner lists, per category."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:130
msgid "Needs your review"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:130
msgid "Cookies the scan found but could not recognise. Nothing is shown to visitors until you decide. \"Only found in your browser\" means none of your pages set it during the scan: it probably comes from your admin tools or a browser extension."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:131
msgid "Choose a category, then click Approve. The cookie joins the list visitors see. If \"Ask again when the cookie list changes\" is on, this starts a new banner version."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:132
msgid "Ignore / Ignore all"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:132
msgid "Hides a cookie that is not part of your website. It is not reported again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:133
msgid "Two steps. First the server reads your pages like a first-time visitor (all pages of a small website; 40 to 80 of a big one, main pages first). Then the same pages open in hidden frames in your own browser with everything allowed, so cookies set by scripts and embedded services are found too. Cookies your browser already had count only if a page sets them. It takes one to two minutes; if you leave the page, it continues the next time you open a plugin screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:134
msgid "Your cookie list"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:134
msgid "Everything visitors see, grouped by category. \"Automatic\" means the plugin added it, \"Added by you\" means you did. Edit changes category, provider, purpose or duration; Delete removes it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:135
msgid "For cookies a scan cannot see. A * in the name matches anything, so _ga_* covers _ga_ABC123."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:136
msgid "Add all cookies of a known service"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:136
msgid "Adds the usual cookies of a service such as Google Analytics in one click."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:137
msgid "Services found on your pages, \"Other third-party files\" (files from other websites the plugin does not know, so they are not blocked) and the pages checked. The daily email points here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:148
msgid "A bar at the bottom or top, a box in a corner, or a window in the centre of the page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:149
msgid "Compact (default): your text and Allow all, Deny and Customize. Detailed: the window with tabs opens straight away."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:150
msgid "What visitors see"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:150
msgid "The detailed window has three tabs. Consent: your text and a switch per category. Details: every category with its providers and cookies. About: what cookies are, and the visitor's own choice, date, consent ID and banner version."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:151
msgid "Four orders to choose from. Allow all, Deny and Allow selection always look exactly the same, which is what makes any order fair."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:152
msgid "A small button visible after the choice, so visitors can change their mind: a round icon in a corner, or a slim \"Cookies\" tab at the bottom or on an edge."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:153
msgid "Colours and rounded corners"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:153
msgid "Match the banner to your brand. Accept and Reject always share one style."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:154
msgid "Rename a category, rewrite its description, or hide one your website does not need."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:155
msgid "Words visitors see"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:155
msgid "Every sentence and button label. Leave a field empty to keep the default, which is translated automatically."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:156
msgid "Custom CSS"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:156
msgid "Extra styles for the banner. Classes start with sccm-."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:167
#: includes/admin/views/tab-settings.php:40
msgid "Remember the choice for"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:167
msgid "How long a visitor is left alone before the banner shows again (at most 395 days, browsers do not keep a cookie longer; 0 forgets the choice when the browser closes)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:168
#: includes/admin/views/tab-settings.php:55
msgid "Ask again when the cookie list changes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:168
msgid "A new cookie in the list, or a cookie moved to another category, starts a new banner version, so visitors who agreed to the older list are asked again. A scan that finds nothing new never asks again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:169
msgid "Do not ask again after a Reject"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:169
msgid "A waiting period (in days) after a visitor refuses, so you do not nag them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:170
#: includes/admin/views/tab-settings.php:57
msgid "Reload the page when consent is withdrawn"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:170
#: includes/admin/views/tab-settings.php:57
msgid "A script that already ran cannot be stopped, so the page reloads to stop it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:171
msgid "Browser privacy signal (GPC)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:171
msgid "Some browsers send \"do not sell or share my data\". It is honoured: the chosen categories stay off, no banner is shown, and the choice is recorded."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:172
msgid "Tells Google Analytics and Google Ads what the visitor allowed. Strict blocks Google tags until consent; Advanced lets them load without cookies. Leave it on Strict unless your marketing team asks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:173
msgid "Google Tag Manager / Analytics ID"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:173
msgid "Optional. Enter an ID and the plugin loads the tag with correct consent handling. Leave it empty if your theme or another plugin already adds it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:174
msgid "Automatic blocking and your own rules"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:174
msgid "Switches off scripts, videos, maps and fonts of known services until the visitor allows their category. Add an address under \"Your own blocking rules\" to block something the plugin does not know."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:175
msgid "Scan my website / Learn from visitors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:175
msgid "How often your website is scanned, and whether visitors' browsers may report cookies (names only, never values, never from logged-in users, only after enough different visitors report the same cookie: default 2 within 14 days)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:176
msgid "Daily email"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:176
msgid "Once a day, at the time you choose, one email when something changed in the last 24 hours: cookies added, cookies waiting for review, or new third-party files. No changes, no email."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:177
msgid "Consent records"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:177
msgid "Whether to keep a record of every choice, how the visitor's IP address is stored (shortened with ***, a one-way code, in full, or not at all), and how many months records are kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:188
msgid "The table"
